	"checklist.items.flight_international_rule.passport_validity.longDescription": "Most countries require your passport to have at least six months of validity remaining from the date of entry. Airlines often follow the same rule during check-in.\n\nSome destinations, such as the United States for Japanese passport holders, may allow entry even with shorter validity due to bilateral agreements. Short-term stays or specific visa types may also have different requirements.\n\nTo avoid unexpected issues, always double-check the expiration date, calculate whether six months remain from your departure date, and review the latest entry rules on the official website of the destination’s embassy or consulate.",
	"checklist.items.flight_international_rule.flight_ticket.title": "Print or Prepare Mobile Flight Ticket",
	"checklist.items.flight_international_rule.flight_ticket.description": "E-ticket receipt or boarding pass via app",
	"checklist.items.flight_international_rule.online_checkin.title": "Online Check-in (24 hours before)",
	"checklist.items.flight_international_rule.online_checkin.description": "For seat selection and shorter boarding time",
