	"checklist.items.duty_free_rule.duty_free_eligibility.description": "Duty-free conditions vary by country",
	"checklist.items.shopping_rule.eco_bag_folding.title": "Eco Bag & Folding Bag",
	"checklist.items.shopping_rule.eco_bag_folding.description": "Convenient for souvenirs",
	"checklist.items.shopping_rule.cash_souvenir_budget.title": "Cash (Souvenir Budget)",
	"checklist.items.shopping_rule.cash_souvenir_budget.description": "Some markets and small shops don't accept cards",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.hotel_confirmation_print.title": "Print Hotel Reservation Confirmation",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.hotel_confirmation_print.description": "May be required at check-in",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.hotel_confirmation_print.longDescription": "Although most hotels accept digital confirmations, some properties still prefer or require a printed copy. In regions with unstable mobile data or when arriving late at night, a paper copy can prevent delays during check-in. Keeping both a printed version and an offline PDF ensures you can present your booking details anytime.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.passport_copy.title": "Passport Copy",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.passport_copy.description": "Some hotels accept copies instead of originals",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.passport_copy.longDescription": "While hotels typically require the original passport for check-in, carrying a photocopy during your trip is useful. You can leave the original safely stored in your room and use the copy for identification when exploring the area. It also helps expedite procedures if your passport is lost or stolen. Note that some countries strictly require the original in certain situations.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.cash_deposit.title": "Cash (for Deposit)",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.cash_deposit.description": "Credit cards are also acceptable",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.cash_deposit.longDescription": "Many hotels request a security deposit to cover incidentals such as minibar use or potential room damage. Most establishments handle this with a credit card hold, but smaller inns and guesthouses may only accept cash. The amount varies by country and hotel class. Since credit card holds can take time to be released, carrying a small amount of local currency is helpful.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.underwear_days.title": "Underwear × {count} days",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.underwear_days.description": "Prepare underwear for the number of nights",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.underwear_days.longDescription": "Prepare enough underwear based on the length of your trip. Hot climates and active travel often require more changes than expected. If you prefer to travel light, consider using the hotel’s laundry service, nearby laundromats, or hand-washing with portable detergent. Comfort is essential, so plan generously.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.socks_days.title": "Socks × {count} days",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.socks_days.description": "Prepare socks for the number of nights",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.socks_days.longDescription": "For trips involving long walks, socks tend to wear out quickly and absorb moisture. Bringing a couple of extra pairs helps keep your feet comfortable and reduces the chance of blisters. Rainy destinations or outdoor activities benefit from even more backups.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.shampoo_body_soap.title": "Shampoo & Body Soap",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.shampoo_body_soap.description": "Check hotel amenities",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.shampoo_body_soap.longDescription": "Many hotels offer amenities, but the quality and scent can vary widely. If you have sensitive skin or prefer a specific fragrance, packing small travel bottles of your usual shampoo or body soap ensures comfort. Solid or concentrated products are convenient for reducing liquid weight in your luggage.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.toothbrush_toothpaste.title": "Toothbrush & Toothpaste",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.toothbrush_toothpaste.description": "May not be available in amenities",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.toothbrush_toothpaste.longDescription": "In many Western hotels, toothbrushes are not provided as part of standard amenities. Even when available, the quality may not match what you are used to. Bringing your own toothbrush and a compact tube of toothpaste guarantees consistent comfort throughout your stay.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.portable_detergent.title": "Portable Laundry Detergent",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.portable_detergent.description": "Convenient for long stays",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.portable_detergent.longDescription": "Useful for long trips or when you want to pack light. Portable detergents, especially gel or sheet types, allow easy hand-washing of essentials like socks and underwear in your hotel sink. Combined with a drying rope, you can refresh your clothes with minimal effort.",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.laundry_clips_rope.title": "Laundry Clips & Rope",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.laundry_clips_rope.description": "For room drying",
	"checklist.items.check_in_rule.laundry_clips_rope.longDescription": `Hotels may have limited drying space.  
Rope types are lightweight and easy to use in any room.`,
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.forgotten_items_check.title": "Check for Forgotten Items (Drawer, Safe, Bathroom)",
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.forgotten_items_check.description": "Always check before checkout",
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.forgotten_items_check.longDescription": "The final minutes before check-out are when items are most frequently forgotten. Pay special attention to three key places: the safe for passports and cash, the bathroom for toiletries, and the drawers for chargers or medication. A quick final walk-through significantly reduces the risk of leaving belongings behind.",
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.minibar_check.title": "Check Refrigerator Contents",
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.minibar_check.description": "Minibar consumption incurs additional charges",
	"checklist.items.check_out_rule.minibar_check.longDescription": "Minibar charges are automatically added to your bill upon checkout based on what appears to be consumed. Errors or miscounts can occasionally occur. Reviewing the minibar at the start and end of your stay helps prevent unexpected charges.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tent.title": "Tent",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tent.description": "If campsite has no facilities",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tent.longDescription": "A tent serves as your primary shelter during camping. Key factors include ease of setup, resistance to wind and rain, and overall durability. Beginners may prefer simple dome or instant-setup designs, while lightweight models are ideal for long-distance travel or hiking. Choose a tent that matches your environment and comfort needs.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.sleeping_bag.title": "Sleeping Bag",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.sleeping_bag.description": "Choose according to temperature",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.sleeping_bag.longDescription": "Sleeping bags vary greatly in comfort depending on nighttime temperatures. Check both the comfort rating and limit rating when selecting one. Mountain areas can become unexpectedly cold. Down offers excellent warmth and packability but requires extra care in humid environments.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.mat_airmat.title": "Mat & Air Mattress",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.mat_airmat.description": "Protection from ground cold",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.mat_airmat.longDescription": "Sleeping directly on the ground leads to heat loss and discomfort. Mats provide insulation, measured by the R-value, and improve sleep quality. Air mats are lightweight and compact, while closed-cell foam mats offer durability. Choose based on temperature, terrain, and pack size.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.flashlight_headlamp.title": "Flashlight & Headlamp",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.flashlight_headlamp.description": "Nighttime lighting",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.flashlight_headlamp.longDescription": "A reliable light source is essential for nighttime movement, cooking, or emergencies. Headlamps are especially convenient because they free both hands. Consider factors such as brightness, battery life, charging type, and water resistance. Carrying a spare battery or power source is recommended.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.bbq_stove.title": "BBQ Stove & Gas Burner",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.bbq_stove.description": "Cooking equipment (check campsite rules)",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.bbq_stove.longDescription": "A stove or grill is necessary for outdoor cooking, but each campsite has different rules regarding fire use. Some prohibit open flames or restrict charcoal. Gas stoves are convenient and clean to operate. Always check local regulations and choose a stove suitable for the environment.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tableware_cutlery.title": "Tableware & Cutlery",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tableware_cutlery.description": "Disposable or washable",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.tableware_cutlery.longDescription": "Tableware improves comfort during meals and comes in various materials. Titanium is lightweight and strong, resin options are affordable, and stainless steel offers stability. Disposable sets are useful when you want to avoid washing dishes or reduce the amount you carry on the way back.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.insect_repellent.title": "Insect Repellent",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.insect_repellent.description": "Mosquito & insect protection",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.insect_repellent.longDescription": "Insects are common in natural environments, so repellent is important for comfort and safety. Consider mild formulas for sensitive skin and choose formats—spray, cream, sheet, or wearable types—based on your preference. Different areas may have mosquitoes, midges, or other insects, so prepare accordingly.",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.first_aid_kit.title": "First Aid Kit",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.first_aid_kit.description": "First aid for scrapes & burns",
	"checklist.items.camping_rule.first_aid_kit.longDescription": "Minor injuries such as cuts, blisters, or insect bites are common during outdoor activities. A compact first aid kit with essentials like bandages, antiseptic wipes, gauze, and anti-itch cream helps you handle unexpected situations quickly. Keeping it organized ensures quick access when needed.",
	"checklist.items.hiking_rule.trekking_shoes.title": "Trekking Shoes",
	"checklist.items.hiking_rule.trekking_shoes.description": "Shoes suitable for mountain trails",
	"checklist.items.hiking_rule.rainwear.title": "Rainwear",
